module provides a simulation model for an all-digital phase-locked loop (ADPLL) that generates a clock signal synchronized to a reference input. The ADPLL "measures" the period of the reference signal REF and "adjusts" its internal clock period accordingly. The clock generation can be enabled or disabled via the ENb_VCO signal. The key input signals are REF, which serves as the reference clock, and ENb_VCO, controlling the clock generation. The output CLK is the generated clock signal whose period is derived from the REF signal. 
The design uses non-synthesizable simulation constructs to model the clock generation behavior.
