module implements a 3-to-1 multiplexer with an additional default case, selecting between four possible 32-bit inputs based on a 2-bit control signal. The design is combinational, meaning the output is determined immediately by the current input values without any sequential logic or clock dependency. The 2-bit select signal s determines which of the inputs a, b, or c is passed to the output y, with the default case assigning y to zero when s is 11. The circuit uses a single assign statement with a ternary operator to handle all possible cases of s, ensuring concise and efficient logic. 
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module Mux_3_by_1(
    input [31:0] a,b,c,
    input [1:0] s,
    output [31:0] y
    );
    assign y = (s[1] & s[0]) ? c : (s[1] & ~s[0]) ? b : (~s[1] & s[0]) ? a : 32'b0;
endmodule

