This is a hardware design for a module that generates a scrolling text display with sine scrolling. It uses a state machine to load characters, adjusts their positions, clips them to the visible area, and draws them pixel by pixel. The module interfaces with an external system to control the rendering and outputs the pixel data. It also provides a status signal indicating when drawing is complete. 
`timescale 1ns/1ns
module render_sinescroll #(
    parameter CORDW=16,       
    parameter GREET_FILE="",  
    parameter FONT_FILE="",   
    parameter SIN_FILE="",    
    parameter SIN_SHIFT=3,    
    parameter FB_WIDTH=320,   
    parameter FB_HEIGHT=180   
    ) (
    input  wire logic clk,                      
    input  wire logic rst,                      
    input  wire logic oe,                       
    input  wire logic start,                    
