module implements an 8-to-1 multiplexer at the gate level, designed to select one of eight input signals (A through H) based on three select inputs (S0, S1, S2) and produce the selected signal at the output Y. The multiplexer is a combinational circuit, meaning its output depends solely on the current input values and does not require any clock or reset signals. The select inputs S0, S1, and S2 determine which of the eight data inputs is connected to the output Y through a combination of logical AND and OR operations. Each data input is gated with a specific combination of the select signals, where some are inverted to ensure only one input is active at a time. The final output Y is computed by ORing the results of these AND operations, effectively selecting and passing through the desired input signal based on the binary value of the select inputs. The circuit operates without any registers or sequential logic, making it purely combinational and straightforward to implement based on the provided gate-level description.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module Mux8to1GateLevel(
input wire A,
input wire B,
input wire C,
input wire D,
input wire E,
input wire F,
input wire G,
input wire H,
input wire S0,
input wire S1,
input wire S2,
output wire Y
);
